  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Skating course with full turns and give-and-go",
  "description": "Place three cones in a row from your own half up towards the goal and a fourth cone along the board level with the penalty area. The players queue below the cones. One coach stands in the middle with balls for the give-and-go, another coach puts out balls for the finish. Goalkeeper in goal.\n\nA skates forwards along the cones and makes a full turn to the right in the gap between the first and second cone and a full turn to the left between the second and third. After the last cone A gets a pass from the coach and plays it straight back. A carries on round the fourth cone, takes the ball lying there and shoots at the goalkeeper. The next player starts when A has done the give-and-go. Anyone who shoots wide fetches their own ball.\n\nSwitch sides after a while so the give-and-go goes the other way. Progression: A carries the ball the whole course and does the turns with it. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Turns both ways – train your weak side too."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Stick on the ice the whole time so you are ready for the pass."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Play the give-and-go back first time and skate on at full speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Look at the ball when you shoot and follow up the shot."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "main",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "focus": [
    "conditioning",
    "passing",
    "shooting"
  ],
